+// ---------------------------------------------------------------- property tests (randomized, deterministic)
+//
+// A simulated world (battery with glitches/sags/cut-off, USB, receiver link + RC switch, button with
+// bounces and EMI spikes, CLI sessions, MSP_SET_MOTOR, foreign motor writes, arming, feature 3D,
+// reboots and power cycles, millis() close to 2^31 / 2^32) drives the real module every 20 ms for
+// thousands of random sequences with random settings inside their CLI ranges. An oracle, written from
+// docs/settings.md and the module's documented constants, checks invariants on every tick in "true"
+// 64-bit time, so 32-bit wrap problems of the module show up as differences.
+// Fixed seeds: a failure prints the seed, the sequence number, the settings and the event log.
+// Validation (2026-10-20): with the eight AutostartFindingTest findings below fixed in a scratch copy of
+// fc/autostart.c this test passes (no false alarms); 23 of 24 hand-made mutants of that fixed copy are caught
+// (RX confirm 100 ms, power confirm 100 ms, ramp/run time one tick long, mask ignored, limit ignored, ESC 2 s,
+// no USB/arming/3D inhibit, ...); the one survivor (output reading the live throttle) cannot happen on the board
+// because the live config only changes inside a CLI session, which stops the program first.
+// Fixes of 2026-10-20 (P1-P8, F1-F13): the module passes; the oracle now also mirrors the battery hysteresis
+// (F6), the fast unplug with a USB host (F7), gusts never below the steady level (F9), the 1..249 cut-off raised
+// to 250 (F13), the strict 60 ms debounce (P8), and checks (compiled with USE_DSHOT) the ESC beacon only without
+// a receiver (F11), extended telemetry once per battery and never into the stock gate (F4), and the computer
+// hook stopping only the program's own motors (F8). On the module before those fixes it reports 23 invariants.
+// Run alone: test_autostart_unittest with --gtest_filter=AutostartPropertyTest.* (about 7 s).
+
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdarg>
+#include <math.h>
